                                          </div>
                                          <div class="expanding_spirit left_padding_of_half_a_dozen">
                                                <h2 class="darkest_grey_text large_font_style title-font balanced_style bottom_margin_of_two">Designed around everyday life</h2>
                                                <p class="calm_flow foundational_text">
                                                      A room should respond to the people who use it, not only to a photograph or passing trend. Considering routines, storage needs, movement through the space and the activities that take place there gives design decisions a useful starting point. From the arrangement of furniture to the way a room connects with adjoining areas, practical details can shape how comfortable and intuitive a home feels. Blue Door Interiors places these everyday
                                                      considerations alongside visual character, so that a considered interior can feel personal as well as purposeful.
                                                </p>
