            <div id="b601aa">
                  <div class="pure_canvas vertical_border">
                        <div class="centered_horizontally maximum_width_of_seven_heavens sixfold_horizontal_padding twenty_fourfold_vertical_padding small_thirty_twofold_vertical_padding large_eightfold_horizontal_padding large_fortyfold_vertical_padding">
                              <div class="centered_horizontally maximum_width_of_four_elements vertical_division tenfold_division_of_shade">
                                    <h2 class="double_xl_text strong_signature tenfold_spacing close_tracking darkest_grey_text">Frequently asked questions</h2>
                                    <dl class="top_margin_of_ten vertical_space_of_six vertical_division tenfold_division_of_shade">
                                          <div class="top_padding_of_six">
                                                <dt>
                                                      <div class="flexibility_unbound complete_width beginning_of_partitions space_between_units text_on_left_side darkest_grey_text">
                                                            <span class="foundational_text emphasized_type sevenfold_line_spacing">What does interior design consider?</span>
                                                            <span class="left_margin_of_half_a_dozen flexibility_unbound height_of_seven_stars core_of_elements"></span>
                                                      </div>
                                                </dt>
                                                <dd class="top_margin_of_two right_padding_of_twelve" id="ic7r4">
                                                      <p class="foundational_text sevenfold_line_spacing shadowed_grey_text">Interior design considers how a space looks and functions, including its layout, lighting, colours, materials and furnishings. The details depend on the room and the people who use it.</p>
                                                </dd>
                                          </div>
                                    </dl>
                                    <dl class="top_margin_of_ten vertical_space_of_six vertical_division tenfold_division_of_shade">
                                          <div class="top_padding_of_six">
                                                <dt>
                                                      <div class="flexibility_unbound complete_width beginning_of_partitions space_between_units text_on_left_side darkest_grey_text">
                                                            <span class="foundational_text emphasized_type sevenfold_line_spacing">Where should I start when rethinking a room?</span>
                                                            <span class="left_margin_of_half_a_dozen flexibility_unbound height_of_seven_stars core_of_elements"></span>
                                                      </div>
                                                </dt>
                                                <dd class="top_margin_of_two right_padding_of_twelve" id="ic7r4">
                                                      <p class="foundational_text sevenfold_line_spacing shadowed_grey_text">Begin by noting what works, what feels difficult and how you use the room during a typical day. These observations can help you prioritise needs before exploring visual changes.</p>
                                                </dd>
                                          </div>
                                    </dl>
                                    <dl class="top_margin_of_ten vertical_space_of_six vertical_division tenfold_division_of_shade">
                                          <div class="top_padding_of_six">
                                                <dt>
                                                      <div class="flexibility_unbound complete_width beginning_of_partitions space_between_units text_on_left_side darkest_grey_text">
                                                            <span class="foundational_text emphasized_type sevenfold_line_spacing">How can I make rooms feel connected?</span>
                                                            <span class="left_margin_of_half_a_dozen flexibility_unbound height_of_seven_stars core_of_elements"></span>
                                                      </div>
                                                </dt>
                                                <dd class="top_margin_of_two right_padding_of_twelve" id="ic7r4">
                                                      <p class="foundational_text sevenfold_line_spacing shadowed_grey_text">Consider a relationship between colours, materials, lighting or shapes across adjoining spaces. Rooms do not need to match exactly; a few considered connections can create a sense of flow while allowing each space its own character.</p>
                                                </dd>
                                          </div>
                                    </dl>
                                    <dl class="top_margin_of_ten vertical_space_of_six vertical_division tenfold_division_of_shade">
                                          <div class="top_padding_of_six">
                                                <dt>
                                                      <div class="flexibility_unbound complete_width beginning_of_partitions space_between_units text_on_left_side darkest_grey_text">
                                                            <span class="foundational_text emphasized_type sevenfold_line_spacing">Do I need to decide everything at once?</span>
                                                            <span class="left_margin_of_half_a_dozen flexibility_unbound height_of_seven_stars core_of_elements"></span>
                                                      </div>
                                                </dt>
                                                <dd class="top_margin_of_two right_padding_of_twelve" id="ic7r4">
                                                      <p class="foundational_text sevenfold_line_spacing shadowed_grey_text">Not necessarily. It can help to establish priorities and a broad design direction first, then consider individual choices in context. The right pace depends on the project, the space and the decisions involved.</p>
                                                </dd>
                                          </div>
                                    </dl>
                              </div>
                        </div>
                  </div>
            </div>
